From: Freifunk im Neanderland <projekt@neanderfunk.de>
Subject: ag71xx (ar71xx): do not BUG() when the RX ring runs out of refilled buffers

Port of our ath79 patch (gluon-patches-hardware v2025.1.x,
kernel/950-ag71xx-rx-ring-exhausted-no-bug.patch) to the ar71xx driver of
OpenWrt 19.07, for the 4/32 devices of the Neanderfunk "Sackgasse" build.

Under memory pressure the RX refill in ag71xx_ring_rx_refill() fails, and
once every descriptor has been consumed the RX loop hits ag71xx_assert(0),
which is BUG() and panics in interrupt context (seen on a 64 MB Archer C25
with the ath79 driver; the ar71xx driver has the identical assertion). The
driver already has a recovery path: ag71xx_poll() prints "out of memory",
completes NAPI and arms oom_timer to retry the refill. Break out of the loop
instead, with a rate-limited warning, and let that path retry.

Signed-off-by: Freifunk im Neanderland <projekt@neanderfunk.de>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c
@@ -1091,7 +1091,15 @@
 			break;
 
 		if ((ring->dirty + ring_size) == ring->curr) {
-			ag71xx_assert(0);
+			/* Every descriptor went to the stack and none could be
+			 * refilled: the allocation in ag71xx_ring_rx_refill()
+			 * failed. Stop here instead of BUG(); ag71xx_poll() then
+			 * takes its out-of-memory path and retries the refill
+			 * from oom_timer.
+			 */
+			net_warn_ratelimited("%s: RX ring exhausted, waiting for refill
+",
+					     dev->name);
 			break;
 		}
 
